<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="014" project="visual-host-create-button-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Migrate eventService.createEvent to applyResolverFields + lockAssociation support</title>
    <phase>A: Visual Host + Registry + Event</phase>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-hours>4</estimated-hours>
    <dependencies>001,002</dependencies>
    <blocks>015</blocks>
    <tags>shared-lib, adr-024, migration, resolver</tags>
    <rigor-hint>FULL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>ADR-024 compliance migration of existing non-compliant code; regression-sensitive</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>ADR-migration of existing non-compliant wizard; must preserve existing Event links while adding all resolver fields — high correctness bar</model-tier-reason>
    <parallel-group>A</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Migrate CreateEventWizard's eventService.createEvent off its ad-hoc matter/project-only map onto the ADR-024 applyResolverFields (entity-specific lookup + ALL resolver fields, 5 incl. sprk_regardingrecordnumber). Add lockAssociation support so Visual Host can hide the Associate-To step. Copy the pattern from the canonical workAssignmentService.ts.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE shared-UI developer + ADR-024 expert. Follow ADR-024 exactly (amended by #549).</role>
  <goal>eventService.createEvent writes the entity-specific @odata.bind AND all resolver fields via applyResolverFields; existing Event creation surfaces still link correctly (regression-verified); CreateRecordWizard/AssociateToStep honor a lockAssociation flag that hides/locks step 1.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>eventService currently uses a hardcoded matter/project map and SKIPS the 4 resolver fields (design §5.6, R2) — an ADR-024 violation. This is a correctness fix, not a new deviation. The canonical compliant reference is workAssignmentService.ts (nav-prop discovery → payload → BU defaults → applyResolverFields → createRecord → file pipeline → warnings). ADR-024 MUST: populate ALL resolver fields; only ONE entity-specific lookup at a time (satisfied on create-from-host); use sprk_recordtype_ref discriminator.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateEventWizard/eventService.ts
      src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateWorkAssignmentWizard/workAssignmentService.ts (CANONICAL — copy this pattern)
      src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/PolymorphicResolverService.ts
      src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/AssociateToStep/AssociateToStep.tsx
      src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateRecordWizard/CreateRecordWizard.tsx
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      .claude/adr/ADR-024-polymorphic-resolver-pattern.md
      .claude/patterns/dataverse/polymorphic-resolver.md
      src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateWorkAssignmentWizard/workAssignmentService.ts
      src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/PolymorphicResolverService.ts
      src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateEventWizard/eventService.ts
      projects/visual-host-create-button-r1/design.md
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps>
    <step>Study workAssignmentService.ts as the canonical ADR-024 flow. Note _discoverNavProps + applyResolverFields usage and the post-#549 result type.</step>
    <step>Replace eventService.createEvent's ad-hoc regarding map with: discover sprk_event nav-props, then call applyResolverFields(webApi, entity, navProps, parentEntity, parentEntitySet, parentRecordId, parentRecordName, hint) before createRecord.</step>
    <step>Ensure all resolver fields (recordtype→sprk_recordtype_ref, recordid, recordname, recordurl, recordnumber) are written; verify sprk_recordtype_ref rows exist for the parent types.</step>
    <step>Add lockAssociation support: when true, CreateRecordWizard/AssociateToStep hides/locks step 1 and treats initialAssociation as fixed (design §5.5).</step>
    <step>Regression-test: create an Event from every existing surface (subgrid, form) and confirm the entity-specific lookup + resolver fields are set and the record opens correctly.</step>
    <step>Update/add unit tests per ADR-038.</step>
  </steps>

  <tools>Read, Grep, Edit, Skill(adr-check), Skill(code-review)</tools>
  <outputs>Migrated eventService.ts; lockAssociation wiring in CreateRecordWizard/AssociateToStep; tests.</outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>Created Event has one entity-specific lookup + ALL resolver fields populated (verify in Dataverse).</criterion>
    <criterion>Events created from existing surfaces still link correctly (no regression).</criterion>
    <criterion>lockAssociation=true hides step 1; false leaves it visible.</criterion>
    <criterion>adr-check passes for ADR-024; code-review clean.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
</task>
